        "Content": "Drumrooske Middle Donegal Town F94 PYD0\n\nBeautiful Detached 4 B/r Residence\n\nOnly 1.5 km from The Diamond\n\nSituate in a quiet established residential area, overlooking Town and yet only 10 minutes walk from the centre; also ideal location with countryside walks on it's doorstep.\nConstructed in the early 1900's and extending to 141.94 sq.m. (1527sq.ft.)\n\nGround Floor.Sitting Room, Kitchen / Living, Utility, W.C.; Home Office;\n\nFirst Floor.3 No. Double Bedrooms, 1 No. Single Bedroom & Bathroom.\n\nEntrance Hallway6.12 m. x 1.89 m.\nTiled floor; lower walls timber panelled\n\nSitting Room3.51 m. x 3.48 m.\nlaminated floor; open fireplace with mahogany surround; alcove with seating area overlooking front garden\n\n \nKitchen / Living5.83 m. x 3.84 m.\nsolid pine fitted fitted units (2016) with integrated fridge freezer and dishwasher; built-in electric oven and gas hob; tiled floor, solid fuel stove with back boiler (heats radiators & water); alcove with seating area overlooking front garden, also patio door to front\n\n \n\nUtility2.85 m. x 1.85 m.\ntiled floor; fitted unit with sink; plumbed for washing machine\nW.C.Toilet and Wash Basin; tiled floor, lower walls timber panelled\nX.\nHome Office / Living3.50 m. x 3.04 m.\ntiled floor; sliding external door\n\n\nFirst Floor.\n\nLandingoriginal timber flooring; Hot Press\n\nBedroom No. 13.53 m. x 2.73 m.\n Built-in wardrobes & vanity unit\n\n \n\nBedroom No. 22.50 m. x 2.21 m.\nCurrently used as office also ideal for potential en-suite for Bed No. 3\n\n\nBedroom No. 33.76 m. x 3.44 m.\noriginal timber floor; wall length built-in wardrobes; overlooking front garden\n\n\nBedroom No. 43.55 m. x 2.87 m.\noriginal timber floor; built-in wardrobes and storage cupboards; overlooking front garden\n\n \n\n\nBathroom3.69 m. x 3.04 m.\nporcelain tiled floor, lower walls timber panelled; large electric shower, stand alone bath, toilet, bidet, and wash basin\n\n \n\n\nAtticAccess via stira stairs; floored\n\nPVC Double Glazed Windows\n\nOil fired central heating\n\nGood parking area to front and side\n\nThe front gardens are beautifully landscaped with various shrubs, flowers and trees.\n\nBER - F Ber No: 110895794\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\nAnderson Auctioneers for itself and as agent for the vendor gives notice that:\nThese particulars are only a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees and do not constitute in whole or in part, an offer or a Contract.\nAny intending purchaser or lessee should satisfy themselves by inspection, searches, inquiries, and survey as to the correctness of each statement.\n[OR] Whilst every care has been taken in the preparation of these particulars, and they are believed to be correct, they are not warranted and intending purchasers/lessees should satisfy themselves as to the correctness of the information given.\nAll statements in these particulars are made on the without responsibility part of Anderson Auctioneers or the vendor No statement in these particulars is to be relied upon as a statement or representation of fact.\nNeither Anderson Auctioneers nor anyone in its employment or acting on its behalf has authority to make any representation or warranty in relation to this property.\nNothing in these particulars shall be deemed to be a statement that the property is in good repair or condition or otherwise nor that any services or facilities are in good working order.\nPhotographs may show only certain parts and aspects of the property at the time when the photographs were taken and you should rely upon actual inspection.\nNo assumption should be made in respect of parts of the property not shown in photographs.\nAny areas, measurements, or distances are only approximate.\nAny reference to alterations or use is not intended to be a statement that any necessary planning, building regulation, listed building or any other consent has been obtained."
